+# Isolated local arena adapter simplification
+
+This candidate replaces the fresh arena adapter's duplicate implementation with a
+pinned call to the existing short-E adapter. It is an isolated source copy, not a
+deployment or a new scheduler. The original armed controller, science packets,
+reviews, runtime dependencies and training were not edited.
+
+Baseline commit `968d66b` records the two original local adapters. Original raw
+SHA-256 identities (before Git newline normalization):
+
+- Fresh: `2f01463b53e5c7ba8e71677ff3a470680f86ec6e7decbe28360184a8086c216a`
+- Short-E: `70777653e0a6579b138e5b69cb4139cad09bbaecdda710242f7c0ce8b08a19fa`
+
+Only `main`, `verify_authority`, `arena_argv` and `mode_attempt` change in the shared
+adapter. Their parameters express the three existing differences (two PGN names
+and pair-bound shim path), plus the executing wrapper identity. There are no new
+CLI options or classes. The fresh caller hashes and executes the same captured
+shared bytes, avoiding source rereads and module search-path substitution.
+
+Preserved behavior includes existing protocol/search/count/time bounds, authority
+and manifest identities, source seals and overlay origin checks, strict inference
+relations, process parent/start-ticks/boot identity, canonical GPU/IO identities,
+inherited file descriptors, create-only attempt/log admission, finalizer refusal
+of code 3, and propagation of attempt code 3 as valid incomplete work. Existing
+receipt publication code and external process lifecycle controls are unchanged.
+
+Validation is stdlib-only, with private temporary inputs and mocked subprocesses
+and canonical lease descriptors. The 11 tests include differential comparisons
+against both baseline adapters and an AST guard proving the rest of the shared
+implementation unchanged. Run from this directory in WSL:
+
+```sh
+CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 taskset -c 28 nice -n 19 /usr/bin/python3.10 -B -m unittest -v test_adapter_reuse
+```
+
+No GPU job, model payload, corpus, live output or canonical lock is accessed by
+these tests. They establish adapter contracts, not an end-to-end arena result.
+
+The snapshot has no upstream repository remote. These two adapters are local
+operational sources absent from the inspected public main snapshot, so a public
+PR placement is not yet justified. Deliver the local Git diff and review first.
+Any future adoption needs a separately reviewed source-pin update including the
+shared adapter. Original science data identities and frozen protocol stay intact;
+the existing armed packet must not be repinned or hot-swapped.
